{
  "name": "ground-scorch",
  "label": "Scorched ground \u2014 cinders, ash and fused mineral",
  "type": "graph",
  "parameters": {},
  "seed_int": 73,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "name": "About",
      "type": "comment",
      "parameters": {},
      "node_position": {
        "x": -1400,
        "y": -800
      },
      "size": {
        "x": 900,
        "y": 166
      },
      "title": "About this material",
      "text": "Procedural terrain material: edit AuthorControls (it also sets the linked values in Normals). Size: materials.json sets the ground one repeat covers; nothing here depends on it. Relief is the heightmap's height range as a percentage of that repeat (the game's parallax depth). After changing Relief, set the Material node's Depth scale to Relief / 25. The ...PNG8 groups and the nodes after them only store exact file values; leave them. Export: File > Export material > Godot > Godot 4 Standard into data/models/board/textures/terrain/surfaces, then Reload assets in the game's Tuning panel.",
      "color": {
        "type": "Color",
        "r": 0.18,
        "g": 0.23,
        "b": 0.28,
        "a": 1
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Normals",
      "label": "Physical normal",
      "type": "graph",
      "parameters": {
        "ReliefPercent": 0.0625,
        "NormalStrength": 1
      },
      "node_position": {
        "x": 350,
        "y": 400
      },
      "seed_int": 27,
      "nodes": [
        {
